    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d277">

                <pb facs="0987" n="946" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v10/pg946"/>

                <head>277. Backchannel Message From the Ambassador to Vietnam (Martin) to the
                    President’s Deputy Assistant for National Security Affairs (Scowcroft) and the
                    Commander in Chief, Pacific (Gayler)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d277-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Saigon</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1975-04-29T16:00:00+00:00">April 29, 1975,
                        1600Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Thanks for your message.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d277-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>19 CH46 sorties are most welcome. There is now another lull. Nothing in last 20
                    min. We need the capacity repeat capacity of 30 CH53 sorties to get us out of
                    here. As I recall, a CH45 has about 2/5ths the capacity of a CH53.</p>
                <pb facs="0988" n="947" xml:id="pg947"/>
                <p>We still need the capacity rpt capacity of the 30 CH53 sorties requested in my
                    previous message.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d277-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>It now seems I will spend part of April 30 here—a very small part I hope.</p>
                <p>But I sure don’t want to spend Mayday<anchor n="4" xml:id="d277-f4"/> here.</p>
                <p>Warm regards.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d277-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d277-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Ford Library, National Security Adviser, Backchannel Messages, Box 3,
                    Martin Channel, April 1975, Incoming (3). Secret Flash; Specat Exclusive.
                    Repeated to General Brown. This is the final communication from Saigon.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d277-f2" n="2" xml:id="d277-f2-content">
                <p>Apparent reference to backchannel message WH50788 to Saigon, April 29. See <ref
                        target="#d275-f3">footnote 3, Document 275</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d277-f3" n="3" xml:id="d277-f3-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="#d275">Document 275</ref>. In backchannel message WH50790 to
                    Saigon, April 29, Scowcroft responded: “DOD informed me that the six CH–53’s
                    used in evacuating DAO compound will be made immediately available.” (Ford
                    Library, National Security Adviser, Backchannel Messages, Box 3, Martin Channel,
                    April 1975, Outgoing, 3)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d277-f4" n="4" xml:id="d277-f4-content">
                <p>May 1.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
